  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Carlton, with its unmistakable domes, has been one of the symbols of the Croisette since 1911. A historic palace hotel, private beach, view over the Bay of Cannes: a stay here is above all an exceptional experience.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The hotel's official website (carltoncannes.com) states, on its Sleep &amp; Dream page, "pet-friendly (100 €/day)". It gives neither the number of animals, nor a maximum size, nor the places where they are admitted (private beach, restaurants, terraces). The Carlton has 369 rooms and suites and 37 residences, and the hotel has a private beach, the Carlton Beach Club.</p>
      <p>Check before booking: some booking platforms mention a single animal under 8 kg per room, a limit the hotel does not publish on its website. Admission of a large dog, the number of animals and the permitted areas should be confirmed directly with the hotel on 04 93 06 40 06.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: at this level of service, a phone call before booking lets you get written confirmation of the accepted size, the rate and the areas where your dog can go (private beach, restaurants, terrace).</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Croisette and its gardens are well suited to a leashed walk, and Cannes harbour is just a few minutes' walk away.</p>
    </div>

